Thanks all. Writing down what we know so far, proper RCA to follow.

What happened: For 38 minutes orders-api could not get database connections a=
nd returned 503 on about 12% of checkout requests. A new sales report endpoin=
t held connections while it ran slow queries.
Impact: Partial outage of 38 minutes. About 4,100 orders were delayed and non=
e were lost, because clients retried. No SLA breach. The monthly availability=
 target stayed above 99.9%.

Timeline (UTC):
2025-06-03 08:55 orders-api 4.18 released with the new sales report endpoint.=
 None at the time.
2025-06-03 09:12 Alert OrdersDbPoolExhausted fired. Logs showed PoolTimeout e=
rrors. On-call acknowledged and opened an incident channel.
2025-06-03 09:24 20 of 20 pool connections in use per pod, most running the r=
eport query. Asked the database on-call to review long running queries.
2025-06-03 09:36 Checkout still failing. Raised DB_POOL_MAX to 50 on orders-a=
pi.
2025-06-03 09:50 Error rate back under 1%. Disabled the sales report endpoint=
 with its feature flag.

Root cause: The sales report query held pool connections for up to 90 seconds=
 with no statement timeout. Reports and checkout shared one pool of 20 connec=
tions per pod, so reports could starve checkout.
Fix: Raised the pool limit from 20 to 50 to restore checkout, then disabled t=
he sales report endpoint until its query was fixed.

Follow ups:
- Add an alert at 80% pool usage. (SRE team)
- Set a 30 second statement timeout on report queries. (Orders team)
- Write SOP-DB-001 for pool exhaustion. (Priya Nair)
- Move reports to a read replica with its own pool. (Orders team)

